sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User as User Browser
  participant Client as React Client (Axios / Fetch)
  participant Proxy as Reverse Proxy / Gateway
  participant API as Express API Server
  participant Storage as File Storage Adapter
  participant DB as MongoDB Database

  Note over User,DB: 1. Secure Authentication Flow
  User->>Client: Enters credentials (email, password)
  Client->>Proxy: POST /api/auth/login { email, password }
  Proxy->>API: Forward request
  API->>DB: User.findOne({ email })
  DB-->>API: userRecord with passwordHash
  API->>API: Verify bcrypt hash & generate JWT tokens
  API-->>Proxy: Set-Cookie: accessToken (httpOnly, 15m), refreshToken (7d)
  Proxy-->>Client: 200 OK { user: { id, name, email } }

  Note over User,DB: 2. Authenticated Data Retrieval
  Client->>Proxy: GET /api/products?page=1&limit=10 (Cookie attached)
  Proxy->>API: Forward with Cookie
  API->>API: authMiddleware validates token, sets req.user.id
  API->>DB: Product.find({ userId: req.user.id }).sort({ createdAt: -1 })
  DB-->>API: productList[]
  API-->>Client: 200 OK { success: true, data: productList, meta: { total, page } }

  Note over User,DB: 3. Secure File Upload & Streaming Download
  Client->>Proxy: POST /api/documents/upload (multipart/form-data)
  Proxy->>API: Forward file stream
  API->>Storage: Store encrypted file (UUID.pdf)
  Storage-->>API: Return storageKey
  API->>DB: Document.create({ userId: req.user.id, storageKey, ... })
  DB-->>API: documentRecord
  API-->>Client: 201 Created { success: true, data: documentRecord }

  Client->>Proxy: GET /api/documents/:id/download
  Proxy->>API: Forward request
  API->>DB: Document.findById(id)
  API->>API: Verify doc.userId === req.user.id (Ownership enforcement)
  API->>Storage: Stream file chunked
  Storage-->>API: Stream bytes
  API-->>Client: 200 OK with Content-Disposition attachment

  Note over User,DB: 4. Standardized Error Handling
  Client->>Proxy: GET /api/products/invalid-id
  Proxy->>API: Forward request
  API->>API: Catch CastError or 404 Not Found
  API-->>Client: 404 Not Found { success: false, error: { code: "NOT_FOUND", message: "Product record not found" } }
